AB  - The project new smart bus tracking/safety system will make it safe and convenient to the people to use as the mode of transport. It addresses key concerns like overcrowding, drunken drivers and safety monitoring. The ESP32 microcontroller is the core of the system, communicating with the GPS module to determine the bus's real-time position. The sensors applied are infrared (IR) sensors, which track the passenger's flow, counting the number of people entering and exiting the bus, and an alcohol sensor, which detects the presence of alcohol in the driver’s breath. Where the presence of alcohol is found, the buzzer is sounded off to avoid unsafe driving. All the data, such as the number of passengers, alerts about alcohol detection, and the GPS location, is displayed on the LCD on board and the Blynk IoT platform and can be accessed remotely using a mobile app. It is equipped to instantly report any instance of alcohol consumption or discrepancies in gas levels and maintain a perpetual record of the bus's occupancy and position. The compact hardware integration ensures reliability and provides real-time solutions to enhance commuter safety and facilitate more intelligent handling of public transportation.
