AB  - The smart helmet is a kind of protection gear that improves the rider's safety while operating a bike. The primary motive is to keep the motorcyclist safe. The attributes including alcohol detection, global positioning system, accelerometer, and fall detection can be employed to achieve this. As a consequence, it acts as a smart helmet. The first condition needs to be fulfilled for the bike to ignite, is that the person should have not consumed alcohol, followed by that the eye blink sensor detects the motion of eyeballs and if the driver falls is tired and closes eye for a period of time, then the sensor alerts the driver and when the accelerometer detects the change in motion, it alerts the GPS and GSM and it posts message to their nearby hospital and relatives. The advancement in our projects includes the temperature sensor which alerts during long hours of wearing helmet. Smart helmets can also help prevent head injuries. Some smart helmets can provide real-time information about the force, frequency and severity of head impacts.
