AB  - This paper aims to develop a system to guide the evacuation route based on augmented reality (AR) through mobile application in order to enable people to evacuate even more quickly in situation where there is not much smoke after the fire. At present, there are some mobile applications based on location-based services (LBS). Among them, `Pokemon Go' is a mobile application game, which utilizes LBS with global positioning system (GPS). In this paper, the AR-based evacuation route guidance system is proposed based on conventional Convolution Neural Network (CNN) using CCTV image processing in indoor fire environment. In addition, a simple experiment is executed, and the performance of fire recognition and AR-based evacuation guidance are measured.
